      <h1 style="font-size:2.2rem;font-weight:800;color:var(--white);margin-top:0.5rem">Cyanide (CN⁻)</h1>
      <div class="param-meta">
        <div class="meta-box"><div class="meta-lbl">Chemical Anion</div><div class="meta-val">CN⁻</div></div>
        <div class="meta-box"><div class="meta-lbl">WHO Limit</div><div class="meta-val">0.07 mg/L</div></div>
        <div class="meta-box"><div class="meta-lbl">Toxicity Level</div><div class="meta-val">Extremely High</div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="content-sec">
        <h2>Overview</h2>
        <p>Cyanide (<span style="font-family:'Roboto Mono',monospace;color:var(--danger)">CN⁻</span>) is a deadly, fast-acting chemical contaminant. Free cyanide inhibits cellular respiration by binding to cytochrome c oxidase enzymes, blocking oxygen transport in living organisms.</p>
        <h2>Industrial Sources</h2>
        <p>Primary industrial discharges stem from gold and silver gold-cyanide heap leaching operations, electroplating facilities, steel manufacturing, and chemical synthesis plants.</p>
      </div>
